# Work log before the user commits

When a change fixes or implements behavior in this repo, append one entry to `docs/WORKLOG.md` in the same turn, before the final reply. Do not commit, push, or stage.

Skip the log when the turn only answers a question or does not change project files.

Each entry:

```
## YYYY-MM-DD — Short title

**Problem.** What was wrong or missing.
**Approach.** The technical choice, including what was deliberately left in place.
**Files.** Paths that changed.
**Check.** Commands run and what passed or could not be verified.
**Commit message.** A subject line plus one sentence on why, in a fenced block the user can paste.
```

Newest entry goes directly under the intro. Do not put secrets, API keys, or tokens in the log.
